Yes, search engines may still see text hidden with CSS such as `display: none;`, so it can still be indexed in some cases.

What this supports is:
- hidden-by-CSS content is not automatically invisible to search engines;
- content that users can reveal through normal interaction, like tabs or menus, is generally acceptable;
- hiding keyword-heavy text just for ranking is risky.
